    chore(gitreins): raise evaluator.max_input_tokens 4M -> 8M for OB-GAP-076
    
    Two starved tier2 runs at the same 4M rung on unchanged code and criteria:
    4,051,277 tokens_in (verdict be9b8359) and 4,051,976 (verdict c2f7b0de); an earlier
    pass on the same task cost 462,188. Two starved runs at one rung prove the cap is
    binding, so raise exactly one rung (8M / 200 iterations, the fleet-settled shape for
    live-verified criteria) and re-judge unchanged rather than splitting the criteria.
    
    Co-authored-by: Alexis Okuwa <wojonstech@gmail.com>
---
 .gitreins/config.yaml | 8 +++++++-
 1 file changed, 7 insertions(+), 1 deletion(-)

diff --git a/.gitreins/config.yaml b/.gitreins/config.yaml
index b5b4f78..0744c68 100644
--- a/.gitreins/config.yaml
+++ b/.gitreins/config.yaml
@@ -10,7 +10,13 @@ guards:
 evaluator:
   max_iterations: 200
   max_time: 25m
-  max_input_tokens: 4M
+  # Rung ladder (measured, OB-GAP-076 tick 389 2026-09-18): a docs-only task with a
+  # 3-clause live-grep criterion burned 4,051,277 (verdict be9b8359) then 4,051,976
+  # tokens_in (verdict c2f7b0de) at the 4M rung — two starved runs at the same rung,
+  # so the cap is binding, not a flake (an earlier pass on the same task cost 462,188).
+  # 4M -> 8M (the fleet-settled rung for live-verified criteria: 8M / 200 iter).
+  # Re-judge on unchanged code and criteria; do not split the criteria.
+  max_input_tokens: 8M
   max_output_tokens: 0.4M
   tool_call_weight: 0.1
   fast_track: auto
